.TH CYAML_CREATE_DOUBLE_MP 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cyaml_create_double_mp, cyaml_create_double \- allocate a YAML floating-point node
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cyaml.h>

cyaml cyaml_create_double_mp(double val, ccol_memmgmt_procs_t *mp);
cyaml cyaml_create_double(double val);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Allocate a DOM node of type CYAML_FLOAT.  Unlike cjson, YAML
explicitly supports non-finite values: +Inf serializes as .inf,
-Inf as -.inf, and NaN as .nan.  All three are accepted and stored.
cyaml_create_double() passes NULL for mp.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
val  Double value; finite, infinite, and NaN are all accepted.
mp   Custom allocator, or NULL for default.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
New cyaml node on success, NULL on allocation failure.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cyaml_double_val (3),
.BR cyaml_destroy (3)
